//
// Absolute-truth correctness anchor for GEMM 1x1 ELFs (vs torch reference).
//
// The other GEMM-related tests (test_pair.py, test_packed_gemm.py) all
// compare one ELF against another. They validate ABI consistency but
// would not catch a kernel that is wrong the same way everywhere. This
// test computes the fused matmul + BN + SiLU in float32 with the
// kernel's SiLU approximation, then compares against a non-K-blocked
// and a K-blocked ELF run on the same synthetic input. PASS if the
// relative-to-max-magnitude error stays within the bf16-accumulation
// budget (3% non-K-blocked, 6% K-blocked).
//
// Both ELFs are built on demand into MDV6_BUILD_DIR/build_merged/.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, torch
//
// RUN: rm -rf test_stx
// RUN: mkdir -p test_stx
// RUN: cd test_stx
//
// RUN: env MDV6_BUILD_DIR=. %run_on_npu2% python3 %S/conv/test_gemm_truth.py --shape all
